title: 'Implement RFC-135: compressed blob prefixes'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    Implements [RFC-135](https://polkadot-fellows.github.io/RFCs/approved/0135-compressed-blob-prefixes.html):
    compressed blobs are now typed with dedicated compression prefixes for
    proofs-of-validity, Wasm code, and PolkaVM code, in addition to the legacy prefix.

    The `sp-maybe-compressed-blob` API is reworked accordingly: `decompress`,
    `compress_weakly`, `compress_strongly`, and `compress` are replaced with
    `decompress_as`, `compress_weakly_as`, `compress_strongly_as`, and `compress_as`,
    which take the expected/desired blob type (`MaybeCompressedBlobType`) as their
    first argument. The new `blob_type` function determines the type of a maybe
    compressed blob from its compression prefix or code magic bytes.

    Nodes now recognize and decompress all the typed prefixes, checking the blob type
    against the expected one. Per the RFC-135 rollout plan, blob producers keep
    emitting the legacy prefix for Wasm runtimes and PoVs until the majority of the
    network is able to decompress the typed prefixes.
crates:
- name: sp-maybe-compressed-blob
  bump: major
- name: sc-executor-common
  bump: minor
- name: sc-executor
  bump: none
- name: sc-rpc-spec-v2
